WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.231
The father of Peggy Carter's children has
been confirmed, and all we can say is, we

00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:08.130
need a movie featuring them right now.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.660
Avengers: Endgame screenwriters Christopher
Markus and Stephen McFeely have gone on record

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.810
confirming that Steve Rogers is, indeed, the
daddy of Peggy's two kids.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:22.109
This raises…well, several questions, but
first, a little background.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:26.849
Marvel Cinematic Universe aficionados are
well aware that Peggy Carter, onetime agent

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:31.890
and eventual director of S.H.I.E.L.D., is
the long lost love of Captain America's life.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:37.110
At the conclusion of 2011's Captain America:
The First Avenger, he failed to meet up with

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:43.940
her for a promised dance due to an unforeseen
plunge into an icy ocean, and an even-more-unforeseen

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.140
70-year hibernation.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.680
This haunted Rogers for years, and he was
only given a slight semblance of closure when

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.280
he visited a now-elderly Carter in her hospital
room in 2014's Captain America: The Winter

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.120
Soldier, in which it was revealed that Carter
had married, and had two children.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.030
"I have lived a life.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:07.159
My only regret is that you didn't get to live
yours."

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.920
Carter's death during the events of 2016's
Captain America: Civil War shook Rogers to

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.170
the core, and it seemed as if he were destined
to forever live in the shadow of what could

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.170
have been.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.460
But amazingly, Avengers: Endgame, in which
the team time-traveled to various points in

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.500
the MCU's history to collect the Infinity
Stones in a bid to reverse the effects of

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.759
Thanos' infamous finger snap, gave Rogers
the opportunity for a do-over.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:35.609
After the defeat of Thanos and his armies,
Rogers was tasked with journeying back to

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:41.030
the points in time from which the stones were
taken, in order to ensure the timeline's integrity.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.520
He did so, but in a shocking twist, he then
chose to remain in the past, finally getting

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.520
his dance with his beloved Peggy and living
out the peaceful existence he so richly deserved.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.250
So, what's the deal with Peggy's two kids?

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.389
Markus and McFeely cleared it up in their
sitdown with THR, and what they had to say

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:01.060
will bend your brain in more ways than one.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.060
"Ahh!

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:02.740
My brain!

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:03.780
My brain!

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.300
Raah!"

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.840
First up, McFeely confirmed that the little
tykes were fathered by Rogers when he explained:

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.450
"It was always our intention that he was the
father of those two children.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.530
There are time travel loopholes for that."

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.890
Now, pay close attention to his phrasing:
It was always their intention that Rogers

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:26.170
was the father of Peggy's children, and again,
these are the guys who wrote Captain America:

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.170
The Winter Soldier.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:31.760
Talk about a long game; did they somehow have
an idea that time travel would come into play

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.170
in the MCU years down the road?

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.470
How could they have possibly known that?

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.110
It's mind-blowing to think of the conversations
that must have taken place between these two

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:44.380
as they crafted Winter Soldier's narrative,
and even more so to think that apparently,

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.230
some of their wildest imaginings for where
the Infinity Saga could one day go apparently

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.600
came to fruition.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.430
Markus then chipped in with an offhand remark
that just might mess with your head even more.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.430
He revealed:

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:01.330
"It does introduce the idea that there are
two children who have somewhat super soldier

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.330
DNA."

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:06.950
While this revelation might cement Steve Rogers'
legacy as a super-dad amongst the likes of

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.450
Clint Barton A.K.A.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.470
Hawkeye and the late, great Tony Stark, it's
not the first time Cap's fathered a couple

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:14.470
kids.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:20.130
In the 2008 animated movie Next Avengers:
Heroes of Tomorrow, Steve's son, James Rogers,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.600
joins forces with the other Avengers' kids
to do battle against Ultron.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.340
Not only that, but the What If comics propose
an alternate reality where Rogers hooks up

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.490
with Rogue on the patchwork planet Battleworld,
founds a colony there, and fathers a daughter

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.490
named Sarah.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:39.570
If you'll excuse us, we've got to go write
a detailed pitch for a TV series chronicling

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.560
the adventures of Peggy Carter and Captain
America's super soldier children.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.510
Here's something we still haven't quite worked
out, though: the existence of Carter's children

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.480
was established years before the Avengers'
time traveling shenanigans.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.430
If Rogers weren't destined to go back in time
and stay there, would those kids have had

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.620
a different father?

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.190
Or would Carter never have had any children
at all?

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:05.770
Try not to think about it too hard; we wouldn't
want you breaking your brain on our account.

